# square.tour, but every segment ends at REST before the next begins.
#
# WHY. MEASURED tovez 2026-09-18 on baked firmware 1.20260918.2
# (lag 0.030): 16 camera-scored pivots FROM REST at this same cruise
# land within 0.87 deg mean |err| (reports/tovez-turn-cal-20260918-lag030),
# yet the same commanded pivots inside square.tour leave +7.48 deg of
# net PHYSICAL rotation error over a lap that the odometry does not see
# (reports/tovez-square-20260918-baked, closure 52.0 mm physical).
# The one difference is that a tour's pivot begins while the robot is
# still settling out of a 250 mm/s leg.
#
# This file changes ONLY that: a 0.7 s host-side dwell after every
# segment. Same geometry, same speeds, same constants. If closure
# improves, the error is injected at the leg/pivot boundary and not by
# the pivot calibration -- which is the open question in
# clasi/issues/rotation-error-is-injected-by-the-legs-not-the-pivots.md

MARK leg1
TWIST vx=250 dist=600 timeout=8
STOP dwell=0.7
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6
STOP dwell=0.7

MARK leg2
TWIST vx=250 dist=600 timeout=8
STOP dwell=0.7
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6
STOP dwell=0.7

MARK leg3
TWIST vx=250 dist=600 timeout=8
STOP dwell=0.7
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6
STOP dwell=0.7

MARK leg4
TWIST vx=250 dist=600 timeout=8
STOP dwell=0.7
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6
STOP dwell=0.7
